Special Acknowledgements & Upstream Foundations:

* Linux Kernel Developers & Linus Torvalds
  For architectural inspiration, POSIX system call design, VFS architecture,
  subsystem abstractions, and documentation conventions.
  https://www.kernel.org

* Dennis Ritchie, Ken Thompson & Bell Labs
  For the creation of the C programming language and foundational Unix
  operating system architecture and design principles.

* GNU Project & Free Software Foundation (FSF)
  For the GNU General Public License (GPLv2), compiler toolchains (GCC),
  and POSIX userland specifications.
  https://www.gnu.org

* Rust Language & Compiler Team
  For the Rust programming language, core library (no_std), and freestanding
  bare-metal development capabilities.
  https://www.rust-lang.org

* LLVM / Clang Project
  For the LLVM compiler infrastructure, code formatting (clang-format),
  and static analysis tools (clang-tidy).
  https://llvm.org

* Intel Corporation & Advanced Micro Devices (AMD)
  For comprehensive x86_64 / AMD64 Software Developer Manuals, Local APIC /
  IOAPIC architectures, and hardware virtualization specifications (VMX/SVM).
  https://www.intel.com | https://www.amd.com

* POSIX, IEEE & The Open Group
  For the Portable Operating System Interface (POSIX.1) standard and Single
  UNIX Specification API conventions.
  https://www.opengroup.org

* Internet Engineering Task Force (IETF) & RFC Authors
  For defining open internet protocol standards implemented in Keira's network
  stack (IPv4 RFC 791, ICMP RFC 792, UDP RFC 768, TCP RFC 793, DNS RFC 1035,
  DHCP RFC 2131, TLS 1.3 RFC 8446).
  https://www.ietf.org

* Linux Man-Pages Project (Michael Kerrisk & Contributors)
  For authoritative documentation of system calls, standard C library routines,
  and Linux kernel APIs.
  https://www.kernel.org/doc/man-pages/

* OSDev Community
  For comprehensive hardware specifications, x86_64 architecture documentation,
  and operating system development knowledge bases.
  https://wiki.osdev.org

* GNU GRUB & Multiboot Specification Developers
  For the Multiboot2 boot protocol specification and bootable ISO image tooling.
  https://www.gnu.org/software/grub

* Netwide Assembler (NASM) Project
  For the x86/x86_64 assembler used to compile low-level boot trampolines.
  https://www.nasm.us

* QEMU Project
  For the open-source hardware emulator and virtualization platform.
  https://www.qemu.org
